WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Brazil is South America's largest country, home to the immense Amazon rainforest basin.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Rio de Janeiro features Sugarloaf Mountain overlooking Guanabara Bay and Atlantic waters.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.000
Portuguese is the national language, spoken by over 215 million citizens across the federation.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Traditional Afro-Brazilian culture in Salvador da Bahia is celebrated through Capoeira and Berimbau.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Culinary traditions feature Feijoada black bean stew and Churrasco slow-roasted meats.

